      "created_at": "2019-03-14T10:16:33Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-03-14T13:17:20Z",
      "body": "Three more things remain before we can check the two bottom boxes:\r\n1. *DS Info* does not specify default values for its optional properties.\r\n2. The `\"frontend_params\"` parameter of the *get_frontend_params* method is neither required nor optional.\r\n3. The `\"test_params\"` parameter of the *add_batch_job* method is neither required nor optional.\r\n\r\nEdit: Upon review I also found the following: Some data types are specified to be strings but no restrictions are placed upon them. I think it would be really nice if we could restrict this to match some regular expression. We could make up some regex that could provide a layer of protection against various injection attacks. These are the data types:\r\n* `API key`\r\n* `Test id`\r\n* `Translation language`\r\n* `Username`",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
